    "field_name": "Output Fields / Metrics to Parse",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "direction, transfer_size_bytes, latency_us, bandwidth_GBps. Derived (parse_results.py): bandwidth_gbps_h2d = mean bandwidth_GBps among direction=H2D rows at the largest swept transfer_size_bytes"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Success Criteria",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "parsed rows status=ok and bandwidth/latency gates pass"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Parser and Normalization Notes",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Unparsed stdout falls back to 1024-byte rows with latency_us=12. #1 bandwidth_gbps is still a blind mean across ALL directions/sizes -- the collector does not measure H2D/D2H combined-vs-separate any differently than before. #3 bandwidth_gbps_h2d is new: this component now ships its own scripts/parse_results.py, which isolates peak H2D bandwidth (small transfers are latency-dominated, not bandwidth-representative, so the largest swept size is used). D2H/D2D peaks are computed the same way internally but not yet exposed as metrics"
  },
